    "title": "Observer",
    "profile_status": "evidence_deepened_research_pass",
    "canonical_definition": "A situated participant in knowing and acting whose capacities and distinctions partly constitute the world available for description and intervention.",
    "summary": "The observer is not an optional spectator outside the system. Sensors, language, history, interests and position shape what becomes signal, object, boundary and possible action.",
    "why_it_matters": "Systems work that excludes the observer often turns a local view into an apparently objective system. Including the observer makes responsibility, limitation and alternative views visible.",
